# The composed tree. Not a directory of files but the composition itself:
# built at every session, empty between them. Never committed -- git
# records no empty directory, and a placeholder file in this one would
# make camp refuse the composition. A session creates it.
/camp-live/

# Machine-local, and neither of them is a decision anyone can review.
/.camp/work/
/.camp/storage/
/.camp/reports/

# What used to be here: camp-workspace and camp-notes, ignored while it was
# undecided how to publish them. They are folded in now, with their history,
# and a clone brings the whole environment down with it. The code is the one
# thing that is not here: camp is a submodule, because it is the product and
# it is published on its own.
